1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
A brutal invasion shattered the peace of the Clover Kingdom's capital.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Fire blazed in five areas of the city, and the Magic Knights mobilized immediately to calm its panicking populace.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
They soon found themselves battling hordes of unfamiliar foes.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
This time you're gonna have to come after me yourself!

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Think you've got me beat now, do you?

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,000
No way, boy!

10
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Come forth, help me!

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Now, number two! Say hi to Alfred! Go and get him, Alfred! He's all yours!

12
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:11,000
...

13
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
...

14
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Oh

15
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Oh

16
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Oh

17
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:58,000
That's odd

18
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:02,000
They may be great in number, but they are poor fighters

19
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Who is commanding them?

20
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Why employ such a strategy?

21
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
What are they after?

22
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:14,000
The King?

23
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Why isn't the Wizard King himself here?

24
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
These are the gravers of circumstances

25
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
And yet he fails to do his sworn duty

26
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Whatever errand he was on

27
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
He should have run immediately to my side

28
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
At the first hint that the capital was being threatened

29
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:45,000
His primary task is to safeguard the royal person from any and all harm

30
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:50,000
As our mightiest mage, the Wizard King is responsible for my well-being above all else

31
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Has he forgotten that?

32
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
I assure you, he hasn't

33
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Sire, we of the Wizard King's staff will be here to guard you until he can return

34
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Oh, that Julius!

35
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
We share authority and military matters

36
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,000
And he thinks that means he can do whatever he pleases

37
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Arrogant pup

38
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Sometimes he seems to forget that this kingdom has but one ruler

39
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Augustus Kyra Clover is king here

40
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Not Julius Novocrono

41
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:26,000
What are you still doing here, Chef?

42
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
The capital is under attack

43
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,000
We need to get to safety, quickly

44
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,000
You fool!

45
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,000
I would never turn tail and run during the middle of a dish

46
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
I am a chef

47
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,000
A little invasion won't stop me from completing this feast

48
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,000
All due respect, sir, but I'm afraid the banquet's over

49
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,000
The magic knights have all gone down to the city to fight

50
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
There's no one for us to serve

51
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,000
What?!

52
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
They had the nerve to leave without even trying my entree

53
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
It is a national emergency

54
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Which means we need to get out

55
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Hey!

56
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Where did this little shortcake come from?

57
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
You've mentioned a special entree, Chef

58
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Huh?

59
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,000
I'd be honored if you'd let me try it for you!

60
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:13,000
A magic knight robe

61
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:18,000
She must be one of the big shots from the Distinguished Service Ceremony

62
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Look at her

63
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Those eyes ablaze with determination

64
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
That drool sparkling with desperation

65
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:30,000
This one is something special

66
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:34,000
I hope you're hungry!

67
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Just you wait

68
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:39,000
I'll make you a dish that will ruin you for all other food

69
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,000
You can't be serious, sir!

70
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:45,000
We don't have time for this! We'll die!

71
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,000
I'm not afraid of death

72
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Life is life! Cooking is all!

73
00:05:49,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Poor little brat! It looks like you're having some trouble!

74
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:09,000
That rusty anti-magic sword of yours is failing you!

75
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:14,000
It's nothing more than a hunk of metal if you can't hit your target!

76
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Please don't get hit!

77
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Quick run!

78
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Get away from there!

79
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,000
Okay...

80
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:32,000
But he needs help too!

81
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Everything will be alright

82
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Leave it to me

83
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Don't worry

84
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
I would never abandon someone like that

85
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Come on! Get down here!

86
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Did you really think that would work?

87
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:05,000
He's not going to stand still just because you asked him to, you idiot!

88
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Back when we were in the dungeon

89
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Yeah, I'll bring this guy down

90
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:14,000
And I'll get one or two hits in for you while I'm at it

91
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,000
I may not have any magic power

92
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
But what I do have

93
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
ARE MY FRIENDS!

94
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:26,000
When his sword was imbued with my magic, Asta defeated that mage

95
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:30,000
If I lend him my power again, even an enemy in mid-air should be no problem

96
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Black bull girl

97
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:38,000
If you're going to step in and assist your squad mate, I will accompany you

98
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:41,000
I won't allow that coward to harm my rival

99
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Great

100
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,000
A playmate for you!

101
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,000
That should keep you occupied!

102
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
Such muddy magic...

103
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
Not a good match with mine

104
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Basta!

105
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:03,000
That wound he got earlier looks bad!

106
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Huh?

107
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
Hey brat!

108
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Remember what you said earlier?

109
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,000
That stuff about me coming after you myself!

110
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Don't you get it?

111
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Why would I bother fighting you myself?

112
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,000
I've got plenty of others to do it for me!

113
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,000
I just have to sit back and watch!

114
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,000
That way I achieve maximum results with minimum risk!

115
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,000
The plus son of not being a muscle-bond moron!

116
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,000
I've got plenty of others to do it for me!

117
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,000
I just have to sit back and watch!

118
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
That way I achieve maximum results with minimum risk!

119
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,000
The plus son of not being a muscle-bond moron!

120
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,000
I not only have a brain, but I know how to use it!

121
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Something you can't do it for me!

122
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,000
That way I achieve maximum results with minimum risk!

123
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,000
The plus son of not being a muscle-bond moron!

124
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:31,000
I not only have a brain, but I know how to use it!

125
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Something you can't say!

126
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Hey idiot!

127
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,100
Sorry!

128
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:40,300
And 3% more people have money!

129
00:08:40,300 --> 00:08:42,300
Who are going to even manage?

130
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:43,400
Let them not be a bunch of aructive banana arms!

131
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:44,400
I'll do it for myself!

132
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:48,400
It's pretty Für than about!

133
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,400
I'll have plenty of others to do it for me!

134
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:52,120
I'll do it for you!

135
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:54,540
What should I do?

136
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:57,900
This guy is more of a monster than a human being.

137
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,240
I can't let him win.

138
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:03,660
What are you thinking about over there?

139
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,120
How to defeat me?

140
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:06,860
Stop wasting your time!

141
00:09:07,140 --> 00:09:08,900
Nothing's going to save you now!

142
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:09,480
Alfred!

143
00:09:14,660 --> 00:09:15,220
Asta!

144
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:24,780
Damn it.

145
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:25,940
Now what?

146
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:29,780
Finish him!

147
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:51,660
No!

148
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:53,040
Impossible!

149
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:54,660
My Alfred!

150
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:57,880
Reduced the cinders with one strike!

151
00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:03,140
It was him.

152
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:15,880
What's wrong with me?

153
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:17,800
Why couldn't I beat him?

154
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:19,980
I wanted to do it on my own.

155
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:24,180
I interfered in your fight.

156
00:10:24,680 --> 00:10:25,660
It was necessary.

157
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:26,380
I'm sorry.

158
00:10:26,380 --> 00:10:32,080
I thought it a pity for a magic knight of your caliber to die here.

159
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:38,640
Forgive me.

160
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:47,280
I will say, though, for a commoner with no magic, you handled yourself well against a difficult enemy.

161
00:10:47,280 --> 00:10:49,040
You know, kid, I like you.

162
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:50,940
Come join our crew.

163
00:10:50,940 --> 00:10:51,740
He was right.

164
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:52,280
He was right.

165
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:56,680
It pains me to admit it, but Yami showed greater foresight than the rest of us.

166
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:57,680
Asta, you said you planned to become the wizard king.

167
00:10:57,680 --> 00:11:10,600
You said you planned to become the wizard king.

168
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:13,360
You said you could be the magic knight of your country.

169
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:14,140
What?

170
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:16,480
You think that you could be the wizard king?

171
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:20,200
Whatever anti-magic abilities you have, you're a brainless brat!

172
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:22,200
You'll never amount to anything!

173
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,200
Asta.

174
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,200
It seems that I am your rival as well.

175
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:37,200
Interesting turn of events.

176
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:39,200
The Black Bullboy couldn't handle it,

177
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,200
so it looks like I've got a new opponent.

178
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:46,200
None other than the Captain of the Crimson Lion Kings.

179
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:50,200
The Great Quagolion Vermillion!

180
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:53,200
You've done enough.

181
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:55,200
You can leave the rest to me now.

182
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:19,200
He's all right.

183
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:21,200
My brother's got this.

184
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:32,200
Did he really mean what he said before?

185
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:35,200
It seems that I am your rival as well.

186
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:38,200
A Captain's rival? No way!

187
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:39,200
Wait!

188
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,200
This is no time to be giving up!

189
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:47,200
I'll fight with you!

190
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:49,200
I can keep going!

191
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:51,200
No you can't!

192
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:55,200
Like I wasn't already hurt enough!

193
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:56,200
Exactly.

194
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:59,200
A warrior must always be aware of his body's condition.

195
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:03,200
He must assess whether or not he is truly able to fight.

196
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:09,200
Right now I would say that you most likely are not.

197
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:14,200
Your brash fearlessness may well be the greatest weapon you have,

198
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:16,200
but you must learn to remain calm.

199
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:20,200
That is if you truly do wish to be the Wizard King.

200
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:28,200
Tell me, what is the purpose of this attack?

201
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:33,200
Your actions are too inconsistent for this to be a true invasion,

202
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:36,200
and too organized for it to be some sort of terrorism.

203
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:38,200
Just who are you?

204
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:40,200
You really don't know.

205
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:42,200
Well, I can't say I'm surprised.

206
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:46,200
Though it's a shame I'm the only one enjoying this reunion.

207
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,200
What's that?

208
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:54,200
I was a magic knight, inducted six years ago as a top candidate.

209
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,200
One of us.

210
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:58,200
No, that can't be possible.

211
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:01,200
More than possible, I assure you.

212
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:04,200
Though I suppose you took little note of me at the time.

213
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:16,200
He's a regular citizen, but his power is incredible.

214
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,200
Do we have any hands, Captains?

215
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:25,200
It's been a long time, but I remember you.

216
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:27,200
Your name?

217
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:29,200
The name's Rades.

218
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,200
Rades, that's right.

219
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:35,200
You were chosen by the Purple Orcas, so why are you fighting against us now?

220
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:38,200
Because those short-sighted fools kicked me out.

221
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:40,200
You were expelled?

222
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:42,200
That doesn't make sense.

223
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,200
You were strong, had so much potential.

224
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:48,200
They were frightened by what I could do with my wraith magic.

225
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:50,200
They said it was dangerous.

226
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:51,200
Forbidden!

227
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:54,200
I was exiled not just from my squad, but from the entire kingdom.

228
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:56,200
I'm only an average citizen.

229
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:58,200
No one cared enough to stand up for me!

230
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,200
No one!

231
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:01,200
I was beneath them.

232
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:03,200
It didn't matter that my skills were greater!

233
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:05,200
Greater than the nobles!

234
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:06,200
Greater than anyone's!

235
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:10,200
Magic is supposed to be everything, and yet they cast me aside!

236
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:11,200
Fools!

237
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,200
There you have it, Captain.

238
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:16,200
I'm here to use my cursed power to get revenge on the magic knights.

239
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:18,200
And the kingdom that rejected me.

240
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:20,200
That is the purpose of this attack.

241
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:23,200
Well, that's one of the purposes anyway.

242
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:27,200
All of this just to get your revenge?

243
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:30,200
Don't toy with me!

244
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,200
You fool!

245
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:34,200
You doubt me?

246
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:36,200
Ha!

247
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:37,200
That's the thing about reasons.

248
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:39,200
They're usually quite simple.

249
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:45,200
Leo!

250
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:46,200
Right here, brother!

251
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,200
Do you need any help?

252
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,200
Nope!

253
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:51,200
We've got this under control!

254
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,200
Don't worry about us!

255
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,200
Hey!

256
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:56,200
Alright then!

257
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,200
Hey!

258
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:00,200
You take care of that creature while I handle the mage!

259
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:02,200
Yes, sir!

260
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,200
Wow!

261
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:04,200
These guys are hardcore!

262
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:06,200
Real warrior brothers!

263
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,200
You don't actually think that's going to work!

264
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:11,200
Their magics are too mismatched for a decent fight!

265
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:13,200
Not that I was going to let you help!

266
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:14,200
They're on their own!

267
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,200
That's enough talking!

268
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:23,200
Time to fight!

269
00:16:24,200 --> 00:16:25,200
Flame creation magic!

270
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:27,200
Leo Rutians!

271
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,200
The Wraith shielded itself!

272
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:42,200
Meet my number one, Carl!

273
